TITLE:: Patternarium
SUMMARY:: Stateful and structural Patterns for composition
CATEGORIES:: Libraries>Patternarium
RELATED:: Classes/Pscan, Classes/Pwindow, Classes/Ptransduce, Classes/Pmorphism

DESCRIPTION::
Patternarium is a language-side library. Numerical streams need no server. This development snapshot contains four foundational Patterns and five sequence Patterns. Renewal/Hawkes timing, finite constraints and graph walks are also available. The five experimental models are available; see the Systems Guide.

SECTION:: Example instruments
Boot the server before evaluating this block. These four SynthDefs are optional Help fixtures, installed only when this block is evaluated. Musical examples in the class Help use them.
code::
s.boot;
::
code::
(
SynthDef(\fmPiano, { |out=0, freq=440, amp=0.1, gate=1, pan=0|
    var env = EnvGen.kr(Env.perc(0.005, 2.8, curve: -5), gate, doneAction: 2);
    var mod = SinOsc.ar(freq * 2, 0, freq * 1.6 * env);
    var sig = SinOsc.ar(freq + mod) * env;
    sig = sig + (SinOsc.ar(freq * 2.01) * env.squared * 0.12);
    Out.ar(out, Pan2.ar(sig * amp, pan));
}).add;

SynthDef(\saw, { |out=0, freq=440, amp=0.1, gate=1, pan=0, cutoff=2200, rq=0.25|
    var env = EnvGen.kr(Env.adsr(0.01, 0.15, 0.65, 0.4), gate, doneAction: 2);
    var sig = Saw.ar(freq * [1, 1.005]).sum * 0.5;
    sig = RLPF.ar(sig, cutoff.clip(40, 18000), rq.clip(0.05, 1));
    Out.ar(out, Pan2.ar(sig * env * amp, pan));
}).add;

SynthDef(\mallet, { |out=0, freq=440, amp=0.1, pan=0|
    var exc = PinkNoise.ar * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.001, 0.02));
    var body = Ringz.ar(exc, freq * [1, 2.01, 3.97], [1.3, 0.8, 0.45]).sum;
    var round = SinOsc.ar(freq, 0, 0.12) * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.001, 0.32));
    var env = EnvGen.kr(Env.perc(0.001, 1.4, curve: -4), doneAction: 2);
    Out.ar(out, Pan2.ar((body * 0.22 + round) * env * amp, pan));
}).add;

SynthDef(\farfisa, { |out=0, freq=440, amp=0.08, gate=1, pan=0|
    var env = EnvGen.kr(Env.asr(0.02, 1, 0.12), gate, doneAction: 2);
    var vibrato = SinOsc.kr(5.7, 0, 0.004, 1);
    var f = freq * vibrato;
    var sig = Pulse.ar(f * [1, 2, 4], [0.48, 0.5, 0.52], [0.65, 0.25, 0.1]).sum;
    sig = HPF.ar(sig, 90);
    sig = LPF.ar(sig, 5200);
    Out.ar(out, Pan2.ar(sig * env * amp, pan));
}).add;
)
::

SECTION:: Foundations
list::
## link::Classes/Pscan:: computes a recurrence for every source item.
## link::Classes/Pwindow:: collects lazy overlapping or gapped windows.
## link::Classes/Ptransduce:: emits zero, one or many items per transition.
## link::Classes/Pmorphism:: rewrites complete generations in parallel.
::
See link::Guides/Patternarium-Foundations:: and link::Reference/Patternarium-Protocols::.

SECTION:: Mathematical sequences
See link::Guides/Patternarium-Sequences:: for De Bruijn coverage, mixed-radix Gray traversal, QMC points, rotation words and ten named numerical sequences.

SECTION:: Point processes and graph systems
See link::Guides/Patternarium-Processes:: for arrival-time semantics and distributions. Use link::Classes/Pconstraint:: to solve complete finite sequences and link::Classes/PgraphWalk:: to traverse weighted graphs.

SECTION:: Experimental systems
link::Guides/Patternarium-Systems:: introduces PPM-C generation, Petri nets, Kuramoto oscillators, bounded branching and sandpile avalanches. These APIs may change before 1.0.
